    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the smallest three-digit number that is divisible by both 6 and 9.\nExplain how you arrived at your answer.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "108; the LCM of 6 and 9 is 18, and 108 is its smallest three-digit multiple.",
      "worked": "The LCM of 6 and 9 is 18, so a number divisible by both must be a multiple of 18.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}18\\times5&=90\\\\18\\times6&=108\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest three-digit number divisible by both 6 and 9 is 108.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
